{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_376fd5eb169bc1d4fca22bd22367d440b66e36109077b5ae68d94f9853569cb9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ef020c6d76a275ac841e4892b16b07692cf06bd1452a00d8c5c14a55ff6ca6dc"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Bundled whitelisted scripts include run_claude.sh, mac_health.sh, mac_ram.sh, mac_disk.sh, mac_top.sh, mac_network.sh, process_kill.sh, port_check.sh, docker_ps.sh, docker_logs.sh, git_status.sh, pkg_outdated.sh, and list_scripts.sh, many supporting --json structured output.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b14ee9355faf61670896ab1827815e6130cc0142329fab1639f558b0f17349b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1740bb9445434b194b102748c276b53503f65485a170a82f9fea7a99bd6b3abe","slc_6c91e3cedc9d9a387e5c05002bc24877dac3155618d07b77781b611e19391e72","slc_8ac46cebb72a44acf78a2904c1b0cd2625ac22dfe7713e7b9fc255b37c35c715","slc_9ed9b0e3bf8775b06c084c5a22c7624d5d55619915ae8b0c1c4776737a1ca49a"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"The pip install provides console scripts cowork-to-code-bridge-daemon, -uninstall, and -selfcheck; selfcheck checks six items, prints PASS/FAIL per check, and exits 0 if all pass or 1 if any fail.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7b99b2a3dfcfa7fc57761246e3d61e7cab499a93796f8ce0d730be757c07125e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2fef71fa3265198c5deeb581a9c267536bc3a225202a7c36acdd7207f176b0cc"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"The system has four parts: a Cowork skill auto-loaded in each session, a shared bridge folder with queue/, results/, and progress/ subfolders, a daemon managed by launchd or systemd (or started manually), and run_claude.sh which hands tasks to a local Claude Code agent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_900008f83860e7140c0523c1e44171aa54bd63f4fcac8edf8e28dc53a778cf59","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d138a503fce0b434c0762f79b0b5f4e128d512e6cbc8aee0ea794076193f5912"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"The daemon only runs scripts from ~/.cowork-to-code-bridge/scripts/ whose names match a strict pattern (no path tricks or symlinks), rejects commands with a wrong token, and runs as the normal user without sudo.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_97cfa7fffdce031793ff195f1acb436c544378e67b24b0054b7c3c764c699333","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_beab2d671b9e4542caae5a0c8de2205e39e385556a11b9561e93c7f005362d0b","slc_c3e71616b1b05356315e57ec14d0b200ba79ed9a2473ac800f6441e18e0726c9"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Requests are idempotent: results are cached by an idempotency key so a retry after a dropped connection returns the cached result instead of re-running the agent or script; tasks are journaled and marked in-flight, and a reboot mid-task is detected rather than silently re-run.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9d255167431975fb19ea5cc72fe1ffad59481027c992c72c325c9f6969bc0a42","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_45543003560c93add7407e201b20e1e86ec8b63c67fa313a5fb3a6924cbee2b0","slc_4f04e97b2b0c3290ef944bb7fd345db29b8c502b2ca275ee044f0bc8abd367ce","slc_c58138762c03a007e035f5781eb382c959ee75742d0786c1e8a3970cdc501c4a"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Rather than a network connection, the bridge uses files on a shared folder that Cowork mounts; the README notes this is slower (about one second per call versus milliseconds for MCP) but works because Cowork's sandbox cannot reach localhost services.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9e9dae7fab30ab30bd3389c00ce2bf90e33f4a20ddd2d960156a53835b4c4fec","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_828b09745ddb724c35d36c97f100a2f9ecd54ad20627e7177280fbec314a9934","slc_c33358e9b39b9653d8048df2ec112405e3b6961dfc3bb65432ca91875328e31a","slc_ffbbf5627fb7696517eeae98cce7e3548eda6a396068909f51fcbc9739373bcf"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Native Windows is not supported yet; Windows users must install inside WSL2 (Ubuntu) with systemd enabled. The README also lists threats the bridge cannot defend against, including malicious user-written scripts and an attacker who already has filesystem write access.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a05a1bb40017e0e916c4fd45a07d5af7f297a2ac6503fbdd3b6b942902639302","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2fffa2e9757df06917dec4b288aa03c49ef30640791bc005ea8653a958b04647"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Long-running tasks can pause and ask the user a question back through the Cowork session via request_cowork.sh, moving through awaiting_reply, reply_to_machine(), and resume_remote(), with timeouts distinguishable from approvals and parallel tasks getting separate replies.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bf9bc3f02a084af72fac83d5a60cead846f3680d5db5f7e6576c4c9aafeda890","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_76e9d89b535ef2edbd2f62a4850d2a33e324bc1590a099229582dc038327d381","slc_bcfa11f149ac144ecf6b12f3b4a0363f20bd570883216861fe000d605852801e"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Tasks are JSON files written to a queue/ folder and results are JSON files in results/, with the daemon polling roughly every second; no network connection exists between the Cowork sandbox and the machine.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d2327702b88d5770b2b69066915796c49166159505b04e15df259947b883044e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8692ede7e3c769a5de716954267ebfbe2d4c3b5db587173affbe36cb5c761742","slc_a3df627a8eb7b11c5947c710f265722bb28ee44a47bc96439d9e2a9f98f73a08"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"Per-task controls include a spend cap (max_budget_usd, shown as 2.00 in an example), a permission scope (readonly, plan, edit, or full), and model tier/effort selection; owner-set ceilings (BRIDGE_MAX_BUDGET_USD, BRIDGE_PERMISSION_CEILING) take precedence, with the stricter value winning.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dfa3b744169701f85a8c7d58baa4fc47a03dfc8c14574f92ac8e352dda71d875","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"abhinaykrupa/cowork-to-code-bridge@30b06c2fb24a snapshot b7f65c950b933f92","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_993881ba6c4563f859a9d128dbfdf74e82e0060d4d326755eaf74b1fbf6d7586"],"source_ids":["src_c5d73ac62adb534ca6af196f6c7c5f4a"],"text":"An optional plan-approval hook (approve_plan.sh) gates tasks carrying a plan field: exit 0 proceeds and exit 2 rejects with the hook's message returned to Cowork; if the file does not exist, the plan field is silently ignored.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7c4d13cfbcf04334ba1f18a16fe2f657"}
